        ]
      },
      "worked": "Number cards have ranks 2 to 10. The possible ordered rank pairs are $(2,6)$, $(3,5)$, $(4,4)$, $(5,3)$ and $(6,2)$.\n\nFor $(4,4)$, there are four choices for the top card and three remaining fours for the bottom card. For the other pairs, there are sixteen choices for the top card and four cards of the required rank for the bottom card.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{top 4, bottom 4})&=\\frac{4}{52}\\times\\frac{3}{51}\\\\P(\\text{unequal number ranks summing to 8})&=\\frac{16}{52}\\times\\frac{4}{51}\\\\P(\\text{both number cards summing to 8})&=\\frac{1}{13}\\times\\frac{3}{51}+\\frac{4}{13}\\times\\frac{4}{51}\\\\P(\\text{both number cards summing to 8})&=\\frac{19}{663}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
